# Task
Document the service described by `spec.json` and `design.json`.
- README.md: purpose, quick start (install, run, test), configuration, API summary with examples.
- docs/*.md: architecture (components, decisions with rationale) and API reference.
- Document only what the design specifies; say so where something is uncertain.

- The code and tests are included below. Describe what the code actually does: never claim a
  property (atomic, transactional, migrated, cached, validated, ...) you cannot point to in the code.
  Where the code differs from the design, document the code and say so.

# Inputs

## spec.json
{
  "title": "Requirements Specification: Production Hardening for URL Shortener Concurrency and Database Migration",
  "problem_statement": "The URL shortener service in production suffers from two critical defects: concurrent redirects cause lost click increments due to in-memory read-modify-write operations, and startup schema initialization using EnsureCreatedAsync prevents pre-existing SQLite databases from receiving new tables (such as ShortLinkDailyClicks) across software upgrades.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "R1",
      "text": "The service must atomically increment the ShortLink lifetime click counter and update the last visited timestamp directly in SQLite on every valid redirect without in-memory mutations.",
      "category": "reliability",
      "priority": "must",
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        "Given an active short link with ClickCount = 5, when a GET request to /{code} is processed, then the database row is updated via ExecuteUpdateAsync setting ClickCount to ClickCount + 1 and LastVisitedAt to current UTC without performing in-memory arithmetic (`link.ClickCount += 1`).",
        "Given a non-existent or expired code, when a GET request to /{code} is processed, then no database update query is executed and HTTP 404 is returned."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "R2",
      "text": "The service must record daily analytics using a single atomic database upsert query to eliminate race conditions under concurrent redirects.",
      "category": "reliability",
      "priority": "must",
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        "Given an active link visited on UTC date D, when a redirect occurs and no daily record exists for that date, then an atomic SQLite INSERT ... ON CONFLICT statement creates the daily record with Clicks = 1.",
        "Given an active link visited on UTC date D with an existing daily record having Clicks = N, when a redirect occurs, then the atomic SQLite upsert increments Clicks to N + 1 in the database row without performing in-memory arithmetic (`dailyClick.Clicks += 1`)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "R3",
      "text": "The application startup sequence must replace EnsureCreatedAsync with EF Core migration management executing Database.MigrateAsync() against a handwritten initial migration.",
      "category": "reliability",
      "priority": "must",
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        "Given application startup on a clean environment, when the host initializes, then Database.EnsureCreatedAsync() is not called and Database.MigrateAsync() executes.",
        "Given the absence of the dotnet-ef CLI, an initial migration class annotated with [DbContext(typeof(AppDbContext))] and [Migration(...)] defining both ShortLinks and ShortLinkDailyClicks tables successfully executes and records itself in __EFMigrationsHistory."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "R4",
      "text": "The application must execute an automated legacy upgrade bootstrap prior to running migrations to support databases originally provisioned via EnsureCreatedAsync.",
      "category": "reliability",
      "priority": "must",
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        "Given an existing legacy SQLite database containing ShortLinks but lacking __EFMigrationsHistory and ShortLinkDailyClicks, when the service starts up, then it runs CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS for any missing tables matching the EF Core model, creates __EFMigrationsHistory if absent, inserts the initial migration identifier into __EFMigrationsHistory as applied, and successfully completes Database.MigrateAsync().",
        "Given an upgraded legacy database, when subsequent migrations are applied in future runs, then EF Core recognizes the initial schema state without re-creating existing tables."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "R5",
      "text": "The test suite must verify that parallel redirects executed concurrently record every click accurately without lost updates.",
      "category": "reliability",
      "priority": "must",
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        "Given an active short link, when 100 concurrent GET /{code} requests are issued in parallel, then all requests receive HTTP 307 redirects, the ShortLink.ClickCount in the database equals exactly 100, and the ShortLinkDailyClicks.Clicks for the current UTC date equals exactly 100."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "R6",
      "text": "The test suite must verify that a database created under the initial release schema successfully upgrades without data loss or downtime.",
      "category": "reliability",
      "priority": "must",
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        "Given a legacy SQLite database populated only with the initial ShortLinks schema and containing one pre-existing link with ClickCount = 42, when the application starts against this database, then the application boots successfully, GET /{code} returns HTTP 307 and increments ClickCount to 43, and GET /analytics/{code}/daily returns HTTP 200 with recorded daily clicks."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "R7",
      "text": "All endpoints must maintain existing API contracts, status codes, response payloads, and rate-limiting behaviors.",
      "category": "functional",
      "priority": "must",
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        "Given existing automated regression tests across shorten, redirect, base analytics, daily analytics, and health endpoints, when executed after the atomic counter and migration changes, then 100% of the tests pass without modification to expected status codes or JSON schemas."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "R8",
      "text": "Technical documentation and architectural design records must be updated to reflect atomic updates, migration workflows, and legacy upgrade procedures.",
      "category": "usability",
      "priority": "should",
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        "Given repository documentation describing click counting and persistence, then all sections describing in-memory updates or EnsureCreated are updated to document the atomic ExecuteUpdateAsync / upsert mechanism, EF Core migrations, and the legacy __EFMigrationsHistory bootstrap process."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "SQLite is the production and testing database engine, supporting `INSERT INTO ... ON CONFLICT(...) DO UPDATE` syntax.",
    "The conflict target for `ShortLinkDailyClicks` is the composite unique constraint on `(ShortLinkId, Date)` (or `(LinkId, Date)`).",
    "When atomically incrementing `ShortLink.ClickCount`, `LastVisitedAt` must also be updated to the current UTC timestamp as part of the same `ExecuteUpdateAsync` call.",
    "Existing endpoints (`POST /shorten`, `GET /{code}`, `GET /analytics/{code}`, `GET /analytics/{code}/daily`, `GET /health`) require no schema or route changes.",
    "Database file corruption recovery and file-level SQLite backup mechanisms before startup migration are handled externally by infrastructure/operational tooling."
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    {
      "id": "Q1",
      "question": "What is the exact column definition and unique index name for the conflict target on ShortLinkDailyClicks in AppDbContext (e.g., ShortLinkId and Date)?",
      "why_it_matters": "The SQLite ON CONFLICT clause requires explicit target columns or index names; a mismatch will cause runtime SQL syntax errors during redirect upserts.",
      "blocking": true,
      "proposed_default": "Target the composite unique index on `(ShortLinkId, Date)` matching the EF Core entity model definition."
    },
    {
      "id": "Q2",
      "question": "Should legacy database bootstrapping run within an explicit transaction to prevent half-initialized migration history states if the host crashes during upgrade?",
      "why_it_matters": "A crash between table creation and inserting the __EFMigrationsHistory row could leave the database in an inconsistent state.",
      "blocking": false,
      "proposed_default": "Wrap the `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` and `__EFMigrationsHistory` seeding logic in an explicit SQLite transaction prior to calling `Database.MigrateAsync()`."
    }
  ],
  "out_of_scope": [
    "Migrating database providers from SQLite to PostgreSQL, MySQL, or SQL Server.",
    "Modifying public REST API schemas or response contracts for any endpoint.",
    "Installing or relying on the `dotnet ef` CLI tool in CI/CD or runtime environments.",
    "Automated retrofitting or backfilling of historical daily click logs prior to the date each link was first visited after the daily analytics release."
  ]
}

## design.json
{
  "overview": "Production hardening of the SQLite-backed URL shortener service to eliminate race conditions during concurrent redirects and establish reliable schema evolution. Atomic counter and timestamp updates are performed directly in SQLite using EF Core ExecuteUpdateAsync and atomic raw SQL upserts (INSERT ... ON CONFLICT). Startup initialization is upgraded from EnsureCreatedAsync to EF Core migrations with an automated legacy bootstrap routine that inspects existing tables, creates missing structures, and registers the initial migration in __EFMigrationsHistory within an explicit transaction prior to Database.MigrateAsync().",
  "components": [
    {
      "name": "InitialCreateMigration",
      "responsibility": "Provides the handwritten EF Core initial migration defining ShortLinks and ShortLinkDailyClicks tables along with indices, annotated with [DbContext(typeof(AppDbContext))] and [Migration(\"20260101000000_InitialCreate\")].",
      "module": "src/App/Data/Migrations/InitialCreate.cs"
    },
    {
      "name": "DatabaseBootstrapper",
      "responsibility": "Executes legacy database schema bootstrap: checks for legacy SQLite tables, creates missing tables (ShortLinkDailyClicks) if absent, initializes __EFMigrationsHistory if missing, and records the initial migration within an explicit transaction before executing Database.MigrateAsync().",
      "module": "src/App/Data/DatabaseBootstrapper.cs"
    },
    {
      "name": "AppDbContext",
      "responsibility": "Configures EF Core entity mappings, indices (such as composite unique index on ShortLinkDailyClicks(ShortLinkId, Date)), and database options.",
      "module": "src/App/Data/AppDbContext.cs"
    },
    {
      "name": "LinkService",
      "responsibility": "Implements URL redirection and analytics logic, utilizing ExecuteUpdateAsync for atomic lifetime click counting and SQLite raw SQL upsert (INSERT ... ON CONFLICT) for atomic daily click increments without in-memory mutations.",
      "module": "src/App/Services/LinkService.cs"
    },
    {
      "name": "Program",
      "responsibility": "Bootstraps web host configuration, runs DatabaseBootstrapper on startup instead of EnsureCreatedAsync, registers minimal API endpoints, and exports public partial class Program.",
      "module": "src/App/Program.cs"
    },
    {
      "name": "LinkEndpoints",
      "responsibility": "Exposes HTTP routes for shortening, redirection, lifetime analytics, daily analytics, and health status.",
      "module": "src/App/Endpoints/LinkEndpoints.cs"
    },
    {
      "name": "RedirectEndpointTests",
      "responsibility": "Tests redirect HTTP semantics, atomic click counting, expiration validation, and 100-request parallel redirect concurrency behavior.",
      "module": "tests/RedirectEndpointTests.cs"
    },
    {
      "name": "RateLimitingAndPersistenceTests",
      "responsibility": "Tests rate limiting policies, database persistence across host restarts, and legacy database schema bootstrap upgrade without data loss.",
      "module": "tests/RateLimitingAndPersistenceTests.cs"
    }
  ],
  "api": [
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/shorten",
      "summary": "Create a new shortened link with an optional custom alias and expiration time.",
      "status_codes": [
        201,
        400,
        409,
        429
      ],
      "requirement_ids": [
        "R7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "method": "GET",
      "path": "/{code}",
      "summary": "Redirect to the target URL for an active link, atomically incrementing lifetime and daily click counts.",
      "status_codes": [
        307,
        404
      ],
      "requirement_ids": [
        "R1",
        "R2",
        "R5",
        "R7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "method": "GET",
      "path": "/analytics/{code}",
      "summary": "Retrieve lifetime analytics including total clicks, created date, and last visited timestamp.",
      "status_codes": [
        200,
        404
      ],
      "requirement_ids": [
        "R7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "method": "GET",
      "path": "/analytics/{code}/daily",
      "summary": "Retrieve zero-filled daily click counts for an active link across the requested time window.",
      "status_codes": [
        200,
        400,
        404
      ],
      "requirement_ids": [
        "R2",
        "R6",
        "R7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "method": "GET",
      "path": "/health",
      "summary": "Health check endpoint verifying application and database connectivity.",
      "status_codes": [
        200,
        503
      ],
      "requirement_ids": [
        "R7"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "data_model": [
    {
      "name": "ShortLink",
      "fields": [
        "long Id (Primary Key)",
        "string Code (Unique Index)",
        "string OriginalUrl",
        "long ClickCount",
        "DateTime CreatedAtUtc",
        "DateTime? LastVisitedAtUtc",
        "DateTime? ExpiresAtUtc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ShortLinkDailyClick",
      "fields": [
        "long Id (Primary Key)",
        "long ShortLinkId (Foreign Key -> ShortLink.Id)",
        "DateOnly Date",
        "long Clicks",
        "Unique Index on (ShortLinkId, Date)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "__EFMigrationsHistory",
      "fields": [
        "string MigrationId (Primary Key)",
        "string ProductVersion"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "title": "Atomic Lifetime Click Increment via ExecuteUpdateAsync",
      "choice": "Use EF Core's SetProperty ExecuteUpdateAsync on ShortLinks matching Id to increment ClickCount (s => s.ClickCount + 1) and set LastVisitedAtUtc directly in SQLite.",
      "rationale": "Prevents lost updates caused by concurrent in-memory read-modify-write operations while keeping EF Core change tracking clean and minimal.",
      "alternatives": [
        "Read-modify-write with EF Core optimistic concurrency tokens (RowVersion/ConcurrencyCheck), rejected because concurrent updates would throw exceptions and fail redirects.",
        "Raw SQL UPDATE statement, rejected because ExecuteUpdateAsync provides type safety and translates directly to an atomic SQLite UPDATE."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "title": "Atomic Daily Analytics Upsert via Raw SQLite ON CONFLICT",
      "choice": "Execute a raw SQL query `INSERT INTO ShortLinkDailyClicks (ShortLinkId, Date, Clicks) VALUES (@linkId, @date, 1) ON CONFLICT(ShortLinkId, Date) DO UPDATE SET Clicks = ShortLinkDailyClicks.Clicks + 1` via Database.ExecuteSqlInterpolatedAsync.",
      "rationale": "SQLite natively supports ON CONFLICT clauses; a single atomic query guarantees no race conditions or duplicate key violations under high concurrency without requiring in-memory locking.",
      "alternatives": [
        "Query first, then insert or update in C#, rejected due to inherent race conditions under concurrent requests.",
        "Application-level SemaphoreSlim locking on link ID, rejected because it does not scale across instances and adds significant latency."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D3",
      "title": "Handcrafted Initial EF Core Migration without dotnet-ef CLI",
      "choice": "Author InitialCreate.cs inheriting from Migration with custom [DbContext] and [Migration] attributes defining ShortLinks, ShortLinkDailyClicks, and their indices.",
      "rationale": "The build and runtime environments do not require the dotnet-ef CLI to be installed, yet EF Core can discover and apply the migration via Database.MigrateAsync().",
      "alternatives": [
        "Requiring dotnet-ef CLI in CI/CD pipeline, rejected because dotnet-ef is not guaranteed in target runtime containers.",
        "Retaining EnsureCreatedAsync, rejected because EnsureCreatedAsync does not support incremental migrations or pre-existing databases."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D4",
      "title": "Transactional Legacy Database Schema Bootstrap",
      "choice": "Prior to calling Database.MigrateAsync(), execute an explicit transaction checking sqlite_master for legacy tables, creating missing tables with CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS, ensuring __EFMigrationsHistory exists, and seeding the initial migration ID.",
      "rationale": "Prevents MigrateAsync from failing with 'table already exists' on legacy SQLite databases created with EnsureCreatedAsync, while guaranteeing atomicity if startup is interrupted.",
      "alternatives": [
        "Running Database.MigrateAsync() directly and catching SQLite exceptions, rejected because partial migration failures leave the database corrupted.",
        "Manual offline migration scripts, rejected because the service must self-heal and upgrade seamlessly upon startup."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "T1",
      "title": "Author handwritten initial EF Core migration for ShortLinks and ShortLinkDailyClicks",
      "owner": "developer",
      "requirement_ids": [
        "R3"
      ],
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "id": "T2",
      "title": "Implement transactional legacy database bootstrapper in src/App/Data/DatabaseBootstrapper.cs",
      "owner": "developer",
      "requirement_ids": [
        "R3",
        "R4"
      ],
      "depends_on": [
        "T1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "T3",
      "title": "Integrate database bootstrapper and MigrateAsync into Program.cs startup sequence",
      "owner": "developer",
      "requirement_ids": [
        "R3",
        "R4"
      ],
      "depends_on": [
        "T2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "T4",
      "title": "Implement atomic lifetime click increment in LinkService.GetRedirectAsync using ExecuteUpdateAsync",
      "owner": "developer",
      "requirement_ids": [
        "R1"
      ],
      "depends_on": [
        "T1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "T5",
      "title": "Implement atomic daily analytics upsert in LinkService.GetRedirectAsync using SQLite ON CONFLICT",
      "owner": "developer",
      "requirement_ids": [
        "R2"
      ],
      "depends_on": [
        "T1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "T6",
      "title": "Add parallel concurrency redirect test with 100 concurrent requests in RedirectEndpointTests.cs",
      "owner": "tester",
      "requirement_ids": [
        "R5"
      ],
      "depends_on": [
        "T4",
        "T5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "T7",
      "title": "Add legacy schema bootstrap upgrade and data preservation test in RateLimitingAndPersistenceTests.cs",
      "owner": "tester",
      "requirement_ids": [
        "R4",
        "R6"
      ],
      "depends_on": [
        "T2",
        "T3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "T8",
      "title": "Execute full test suite and verify 100% regression compatibility across all endpoints",
      "owner": "tester",
      "requirement_ids": [
        "R7"
      ],
      "depends_on": [
        "T6",
        "T7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "T9",
      "title": "Update architectural documentation and operational guides for atomic persistence and migrations",
      "owner": "docs",
      "requirement_ids": [
        "R8"
      ],
      "depends_on": [
        "T3",
        "T4",
        "T5"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "risks": [
    {
      "risk": "SQLite database locked / busy errors under 100 concurrent parallel redirect writes.",
      "mitigation": "Configure SQLite connection string with Write-Ahead Logging (WAL) and an adequate busy timeout (e.g., 'Data Source=...;Mode=ReadWriteCreate;Cache=Shared;Default Timeout=30') to serialize atomic writes efficiently."
    },
    {
      "risk": "Partial legacy database bootstrapping leaving inconsistent migration metadata upon host crash.",
      "mitigation": "Wrap the legacy bootstrap DDL statements and __EFMigrationsHistory insert inside a single SQLite transaction before invoking Database.MigrateAsync()."
    }
  ]
}

